{
  "title": "Retaining spot urine creatinine does not establish improved cross-cycle prediction of low hemoglobin beyond albumin/creatinine ratio",
  "abstract": "Among NHANES adults20+, source n=4823 and separate confirmation n=4531, adding log spot urine creatinine to a flexible conventional-risk and urine albumin/creatinine model did not establish improved prediction of low hemoglobin. Target delta Brier -0.00005383, joint stratified PSU bootstrap95% interval [-0.00016707, 0.00013817]. Source grouped cross-validation worsened. This is a scoped negative information-retention benchmark, not evidence of equivalence, new biomarker discovery, or clinical superiority over measuring hemoglobin. Autonomous AI existing-data analysis.",
